# Temperance marker — untrack turn-prose per-turn markers
- date: 2026-11-05
- branch: fix/untrack-turn-prose-markers
- scope-decision: Right thing — stop two tracked per-turn marker files from
  being auto-committed and pushed every turn, which restarts a 12-minute
  smoke. Right way — add the two missing .gitignore lines beside the six
  sibling transient-marker lines already there, then git rm --cached the
  two files. No hook edits here; the upstream cure is up#2366.
- drift-trigger: If this grows past the two files plus their .gitignore
  lines, stop. Reclassifying which marker dirs are transient is up#1235
  and up#1694, not this branch.
- drift-trigger-fired: Yes, once, and recorded rather than argued past.
  Widened from two directories to three: added state/markers/turn-prose-surface/
  alongside the two churning ones. Reason — it is provably transient by its own
  rule text (.claude/rules/compounding-sequence-fresh-analysis.md step 5 says to
  remove the marker after the proposal lands), it currently has zero tracked
  files so the line changes nothing today, and leaving it out invites the same
  bug on the next session that forgets the removal. This is prevention within
  the same family, not the reclassification that up#1235 and up#1694 own.
